1
00:00:19,393 --> 00:00:21,020
"Stay away from me.
Let go."

2
00:00:21,395 --> 00:00:22,522
"Let go of me."

3
00:00:23,439 --> 00:00:25,942
- "Save the phony tears."
- "Just get back."

4
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:31,030
- "Oh, you little fool."
- "You just stay away from me."

5
00:00:37,119 --> 00:00:39,121
"We can't get involved in this."

6
00:00:39,455 --> 00:00:41,707
Hello, Patrick.
How are you?

7
00:00:42,083 --> 00:00:43,125
Good.

8
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:46,879
- So what do you think?
- Oh, it's a classic.

9
00:00:47,296 --> 00:00:50,174
You know, it just gets better
and better every time.

10
00:00:50,299 --> 00:00:51,342
Yes.

11
00:00:51,759 --> 00:00:53,261
What do you think
of my request?

12
00:00:54,762 --> 00:00:57,056
I don't think much of it
really, Patrick.

13
00:00:57,890 --> 00:00:59,058
Really, I don't.

14
00:00:59,308 --> 00:01:01,227
Meaning you can't accomplish it?

15
00:01:01,435 --> 00:01:02,979
Any task can be accomplished

16
00:01:03,104 --> 00:01:06,399
as long as it's broken down
into manageable pieces.

17
00:01:07,149 --> 00:01:08,276
So you'll do it?

18
00:01:09,694 --> 00:01:12,280
Look, I know
that I'm in your debt.

19
00:01:12,738 --> 00:01:15,616
Okay, so we both agree
that you owe me a favor.

20
00:01:16,659 --> 00:01:17,702
Yes, I do.

21
00:01:18,411 --> 00:01:20,788
So let this be
my favor to you...

22
00:01:21,372 --> 00:01:23,374
let it go... the whole idea.

23
00:01:24,041 --> 00:01:25,376
It's just not worth it.

24
00:01:29,589 --> 00:01:31,340
Well, I find this very interesting.

25
00:01:32,091 --> 00:01:34,093
I'm presenting you
with a challenge

26
00:01:34,802 --> 00:01:36,470
and yet you're backing away.

27
00:01:37,597 --> 00:01:39,557
It's very unlike you, Mr. Stiles.

28
00:01:39,682 --> 00:01:40,891
Look, if you must know

29
00:01:41,350 --> 00:01:43,728
I've grown mildly accustomed
to you, Patrick.

30
00:01:44,228 --> 00:01:46,355
You make me sit up
and pay attention.

31
00:01:46,856 --> 00:01:48,566
I'm very glad
you're amused by me.

32
00:01:50,276 --> 00:01:53,070
But what you're planning now, it's...

33
00:01:53,446 --> 00:01:56,782
- Well, it's certainly different.
- Yes, it is.

34
00:01:57,491 --> 00:02:00,786
If I do what you're asking
of me and you get caught

35
00:02:01,537 --> 00:02:04,874
you're gonna spend
the rest of your life in a federal prison.

36
00:02:05,291 --> 00:02:06,667
I'm well aware of that.

37
00:02:08,377 --> 00:02:10,546
I just have to make sure
I don't get caught.

38
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:13,883
All right.

39
00:02:15,426 --> 00:02:19,221
Well, it's been a great pleasure
knowing you, Mr. Jane.

40
00:02:20,848 --> 00:02:21,891
Good luck.

41
00:02:23,392 --> 00:02:25,853
"Well, I... I used
some pretty harsh words."

42
00:02:25,978 --> 00:02:27,021
"I'm sorry."

43
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:28,522
Thank you.

44
00:02:29,523 --> 00:02:30,691
"But naturally, if I'd known..."

45
00:03:08,020 --> 00:03:11,315
Lorelei Martins, 5474B.

46
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:01,884
Need a ride?

47
00:05:02,885 --> 00:05:03,928
You?

48
00:05:19,107 --> 00:05:21,568
Hey, come on. Please.
Just... just get in the car.

49
00:05:22,778 --> 00:05:23,821
This is ridiculous.

50
00:05:24,571 --> 00:05:25,614
Why are you mad at me?

51
00:05:25,739 --> 00:05:27,324
I... I didn't force you
to escape from prison.

52
00:05:27,449 --> 00:05:29,409
No, you just tricked me
into it.

53
00:05:34,706 --> 00:05:35,749
Oh, come on.

54
00:05:36,333 --> 00:05:37,376
{\an8}Wait.

55
00:05:38,085 --> 00:05:40,295
{\an8}You thought it was Red John
that got you out, didn't you?

56
00:05:40,629 --> 00:05:41,672
{\an8}Yeah.

57
00:05:41,797 --> 00:05:43,924
{\an8}Yeah, well, it wasn't.
I did. I got you out.

58
00:05:44,049 --> 00:05:45,425
{\an8}He would have left you
in there to rot.

59
00:05:45,551 --> 00:05:47,261
{\an8}And I took a lot of risks
in doing it.

60
00:05:47,594 --> 00:05:49,721
{\an8}Nobody ever accused you
of good judgment.

61
00:05:49,888 --> 00:05:52,391
{\an8}Well, what about you? You're the one
walking off into the desert

62
00:05:52,558 --> 00:05:54,852
{\an8}ten miles from a prison
you just broke out of.

63
00:05:55,394 --> 00:05:56,645
{\an8}I'm offering you a ride.

64
00:05:56,770 --> 00:05:58,146
{\an8}I'll take you
wherever you wanna go.

65
00:05:58,272 --> 00:05:59,565
{\an8}You can dump me at any time.

66
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:02,943
{\an8}Fine.

67
00:06:06,196 --> 00:06:08,407
Jane, how many messages
do I have to leave you?

68
00:06:08,824 --> 00:06:09,867
Call me back.

69
00:06:17,332 --> 00:06:18,876
{\an8}Hold on, Tom.
She just walked in.

70
00:06:21,253 --> 00:06:22,296
{\an8}No.

71
00:06:23,005 --> 00:06:26,216
{\an8}No, don't inform
the Marshals yet.

72
00:06:26,341 --> 00:06:28,302
{\an8}I wanna bring CBI
up to speed first.

73
00:06:29,928 --> 00:06:30,971
{\an8}I'll call you back.

74
00:06:31,597 --> 00:06:32,639
{\an8}What's going on?

75
00:06:33,432 --> 00:06:35,559
Have you heard
about Lorelei Martins yet?

76
00:06:36,101 --> 00:06:37,144
{\an8}No.

77
00:06:37,269 --> 00:06:39,646
{\an8}She escaped from federal prison
this morning.

78
00:06:40,772 --> 00:06:44,359
{\an8}Your Mr. Jane was questioning
prison transport drivers.

79
00:06:45,444 --> 00:06:46,945
Yes, but no.

80
00:06:47,154 --> 00:06:48,196
{\an8}He wouldn't.

81
00:06:48,739 --> 00:06:49,781
{\an8}He wouldn't.

82
00:06:50,574 --> 00:06:51,617
{\an8}He wouldn't?

83
00:06:53,535 --> 00:06:54,578
{\an8}Where is he now?

84
00:06:55,245 --> 00:06:58,123
{\an8}I don't know. I haven't heard
from him since yesterday.

85
00:06:58,248 --> 00:06:59,541
He hasn't answered his phone.

86
00:07:00,667 --> 00:07:02,336
{\an8}But that doesn't mean
he did this.

87
00:07:03,045 --> 00:07:06,798
It would make it
much more likely, wouldn't it?

88
00:07:07,132 --> 00:07:08,926
Why is this
a Homeland Security issue?

89
00:07:09,051 --> 00:07:10,093
It's complicated.

90
00:07:11,637 --> 00:07:14,514
I mean, if he is with her
he's in a lot of danger.

91
00:07:15,933 --> 00:07:17,225
You know him
better than anybody.

92
00:07:17,351 --> 00:07:19,770
{\an8}Now if he did do this
where would he go?

93
00:07:21,647 --> 00:07:25,609
{\an8}Any place I could possibly think
of is where he wouldn't go.

94
00:07:28,028 --> 00:07:29,696
{\an8}Uh, would you excuse me
for a minute?

95
00:07:29,947 --> 00:07:30,989
I'll be right back.

96
00:07:34,576 --> 00:07:35,827
Has anyone seen Jane?

97
00:07:36,411 --> 00:07:38,622
{\an8}- No.
- We need to find him right now.

98
00:07:38,747 --> 00:07:41,833
{\an8}Put a B.O.L.O. out on his car. Grace, Cho,
I want you to go to his motel room.

99
00:07:42,167 --> 00:07:45,295
{\an8}Rigs, call his cell phone company.
Get GPS tracking on his phone.

100
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:46,463
What's going on?

101
00:07:48,340 --> 00:07:51,051
{\an8}Lorelei Martins escaped
from prison this morning.

102
00:07:51,176 --> 00:07:52,219
Was Jane involved?

103
00:07:53,261 --> 00:07:54,513
{\an8}We don't know yet.

104
00:07:56,932 --> 00:07:57,975
Who's that?

105
00:07:58,684 --> 00:08:00,102
{\an8}Bob Kirkland
Homeland Security.

106
00:08:00,227 --> 00:08:01,812
{\an8}He's leading the search
to find Martins.

107
00:08:01,937 --> 00:08:02,980
Boss.

108
00:08:03,105 --> 00:08:05,816
Sac PD got a report
of an abandoned blue Citroen this morning.

109
00:08:06,149 --> 00:08:08,151
{\an8}Uh, parking lot at 16th and K Street.

110
00:08:08,819 --> 00:08:09,903
Text it to me.

111
00:08:10,112 --> 00:08:11,154
This isn't gonna work.

112
00:08:12,698 --> 00:08:14,157
Well, that's optimistic.

113
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:16,994
I won't tell you
who he is, or where he is.

114
00:08:18,912 --> 00:08:22,040
- Give it time.
- Not now. Not ever.

115
00:08:28,964 --> 00:08:30,007
Doesn't work.

116
00:08:30,382 --> 00:08:31,425
Really?

117
00:08:31,550 --> 00:08:33,427
I figured that when
no sound came out of it.

118
00:08:34,803 --> 00:08:35,846
Yes.

119
00:08:38,432 --> 00:08:39,516
Can we go?

120
00:08:41,435 --> 00:08:42,477
Tell me where.

121
00:08:44,813 --> 00:08:47,858
The ocean.
I wanna see the ocean.

122
00:09:17,012 --> 00:09:18,430
He was leaving a text message.

123
00:09:18,638 --> 00:09:19,681
It's for you.

124
00:09:20,057 --> 00:09:21,600
"Someone after me."

125
00:09:22,184 --> 00:09:23,518
He was being followed.

126
00:09:24,436 --> 00:09:25,854
Looks like he's been abducted.

127
00:09:26,605 --> 00:09:28,899
Jane doesn't have Lorelei.
Lorelei has Jane.

128
00:09:43,914 --> 00:09:49,002
Our fugitive is a known associate
of the serial killer Red John.

129
00:09:49,127 --> 00:09:53,715
She's wanted for murder conspiracy
kidnapping, and weapons violations.

130
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:57,469
We believe that Martins
and unknown accomplices

131
00:09:57,636 --> 00:10:01,098
abducted CBI consultant
Patrick Jane.

132
00:10:01,306 --> 00:10:03,517
Jane led a six-month
undercover operation

133
00:10:03,642 --> 00:10:05,435
that resulted in Lorelei's arrest.

134
00:10:05,602 --> 00:10:08,396
Martins may have kidnapped him for payback
or to take him to Red John.

135
00:10:08,522 --> 00:10:10,190
Either way
we need to find them.

136
00:10:10,315 --> 00:10:13,360
Martins is a Sacramento girl.

137
00:10:13,485 --> 00:10:16,988
I want systematic searches
of old residences

138
00:10:17,114 --> 00:10:18,698
old friends, old coworkers.

139
00:10:18,949 --> 00:10:20,450
You all have information packets.

140
00:10:20,617 --> 00:10:22,119
Study them, and when you're done

141
00:10:22,244 --> 00:10:24,788
contact myself or Agent Kirkland
for your assignments.

142
00:10:24,913 --> 00:10:25,956
Thank you.

143
00:10:26,248 --> 00:10:28,208
- Let's start with Lorelei's mother.
- Okay.

144
00:11:00,198 --> 00:11:01,658
I wonder where they're going.

145
00:11:21,261 --> 00:11:22,512
I'm gonna make a fire.

146
00:11:27,184 --> 00:11:28,685
So, what's this about?

147
00:11:30,020 --> 00:11:32,272
Your daughter broke out of prison
this morning.

148
00:11:32,564 --> 00:11:34,107
Oh, great. Of course.

149
00:11:34,482 --> 00:11:38,069
Have you had any contact
with... with Lorelei recently?

150
00:11:39,863 --> 00:11:42,324
Lorelei hasn't contacted me in years.

151
00:11:43,158 --> 00:11:44,201
Thankfully.

152
00:11:44,951 --> 00:11:49,039
When she does...
it's always trouble. Always.

153
00:11:49,664 --> 00:11:53,168
We have reason to believe
that Lorelei has taken a hostage.

154
00:11:53,376 --> 00:11:55,003
His life could be in danger.

155
00:11:55,587 --> 00:11:58,423
Do you have any information
that you could give us

156
00:11:58,548 --> 00:12:00,717
about where we could find her?

157
00:12:01,301 --> 00:12:03,720
Any, uh, old friends?

158
00:12:04,471 --> 00:12:05,847
Favorite places?

159
00:12:06,890 --> 00:12:08,934
Nope. I don't have
anything to do with her

160
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:10,644
and she doesn't have
anything to do with me.

161
00:12:13,063 --> 00:12:16,107
Do you have any insight
as to how she became this way?

162
00:12:18,652 --> 00:12:21,029
Lorelei only ever cared about Lorelei.

163
00:12:21,613 --> 00:12:23,073
What are you gonna do
with a kid like that?

164
00:12:23,365 --> 00:12:25,533
Well, you don't feel
at all responsible for her?

165
00:12:26,993 --> 00:12:29,496
Now there's a question
from a woman without children.

166
00:12:35,043 --> 00:12:38,630
I've satisfied all my duties
and responsibilities of motherhood.

167
00:12:39,506 --> 00:12:42,425
I mean, look around. Lorelei
grew up in a beautiful home.

168
00:12:42,550 --> 00:12:43,760
She could be anything.

169
00:12:46,012 --> 00:12:47,055
Is this your father?

170
00:12:49,641 --> 00:12:52,686
That's my husband.
He's away in Munich.

171
00:12:53,228 --> 00:12:54,437
He's away a lot?

172
00:12:54,896 --> 00:12:55,939
Yes.

173
00:12:56,273 --> 00:12:57,857
Oh. Figures.

174
00:12:59,025 --> 00:13:00,944
I don't like your tone.

175
00:13:01,111 --> 00:13:04,531
Dana, your daughter
is the mistress of a psychopathic killer

176
00:13:04,656 --> 00:13:06,408
yet you have no information to give us

177
00:13:06,533 --> 00:13:08,535
about how or why
she got that way.

178
00:13:08,743 --> 00:13:10,829
Frankly, I don't care
if you like my tone.

179
00:13:10,996 --> 00:13:12,706
To hell with you, lady.

180
00:13:13,415 --> 00:13:14,541
What happened to her?

181
00:13:14,791 --> 00:13:16,501
Get out of my house!

182
00:13:19,379 --> 00:13:20,422
Thank you.

183
00:15:30,482 --> 00:15:31,650
You should try it.

184
00:15:32,067 --> 00:15:33,235
Water's lovely.

185
00:15:38,532 --> 00:15:40,909
Uh, quickly... go and hide
yourself behind those rocks.

186
00:16:17,446 --> 00:16:19,364
Hello, young man.
How you doing?

187
00:16:24,995 --> 00:16:26,246
Was that your campfire?

188
00:16:27,581 --> 00:16:28,665
No, Officer.

189
00:16:29,625 --> 00:16:31,585
I'm not an officer.
I'm a Park Ranger.

190
00:16:32,503 --> 00:16:33,837
So no gun, huh?

191
00:16:34,630 --> 00:16:35,672
Right.

192
00:16:37,007 --> 00:16:39,551
Campfires are illegal
on this beach without a permit.

193
00:16:41,053 --> 00:16:42,096
It's not mine.

194
00:16:43,972 --> 00:16:45,974
Are you okay, sir?
You seem a little nervous.

195
00:16:46,934 --> 00:16:47,976
Never better.

196
00:16:52,481 --> 00:16:53,565
Are you alone?

197
00:16:57,194 --> 00:16:59,321
Uh... No, she's...

198
00:17:00,197 --> 00:17:02,241
Hi, Officer!
I'm over here!

199
00:17:02,366 --> 00:17:03,659
I'm sorry. I can't come out!

200
00:17:04,076 --> 00:17:06,078
I don't have any clothes on.

201
00:17:07,663 --> 00:17:10,833
Yeah, well, public nudity's
prohibited on state beaches.

202
00:17:11,917 --> 00:17:14,920
Yes, uh, I'm sorry!
It won't happen again!

203
00:17:18,048 --> 00:17:19,842
Promise, it...
it won't happen again.

204
00:17:20,926 --> 00:17:21,969
Sorry, sir.

205
00:17:24,638 --> 00:17:25,681
Okay.

206
00:17:27,933 --> 00:17:29,268
You folks have a nice day.

207
00:17:29,393 --> 00:17:30,435
Yeah.

208
00:17:34,857 --> 00:17:36,191
No campfires.

209
00:17:49,371 --> 00:17:51,248
So where to now?

210
00:17:51,623 --> 00:17:52,666
North to Canada?

211
00:17:53,709 --> 00:17:55,043
South to Mexico?

212
00:17:55,878 --> 00:17:56,920
I'm flexible.

213
00:17:57,671 --> 00:17:59,631
I know a place
where no one will find us.

214
00:18:00,716 --> 00:18:03,802
Take the I-60 East, but I
gotta change my look first.

215
00:18:03,927 --> 00:18:05,137
Find a convenience store.

216
00:18:05,679 --> 00:18:08,640
- I like the take-charge attitude.
- No, you don't.

217
00:18:08,765 --> 00:18:09,808
I do.

218
00:18:10,976 --> 00:18:13,395
Clearly, you've taken care
of someone in your life.

219
00:18:14,188 --> 00:18:16,982
Made all the decisions.
Acted the adult.

220
00:18:17,858 --> 00:18:22,696
I'm guessing you had a vain, selfish
and controlling mother.

221
00:18:23,363 --> 00:18:25,324
But you found
the strength to pull away.

222
00:18:26,408 --> 00:18:27,743
Does she resent you for that?

223
00:18:30,204 --> 00:18:32,456
Patrick, do you really
wanna get to know me?

224
00:18:33,248 --> 00:18:34,291
Of course.

225
00:18:34,833 --> 00:18:36,251
Give the act a rest.

226
00:18:36,793 --> 00:18:39,254
- What? I... I wasn't...
- Yes, you were.

227
00:18:42,132 --> 00:18:43,175
Okay.

228
00:18:45,677 --> 00:18:46,720
"I knew it."

229
00:18:47,095 --> 00:18:49,723
Soon as I heard that kidnapping
report on my radio.

230
00:18:49,848 --> 00:18:50,933
I called it in.

231
00:18:51,934 --> 00:18:53,477
This is the young man
I talked to.

232
00:18:56,063 --> 00:18:58,774
- Was there a woman with him?
- Yes, there most certainly was.

233
00:18:59,024 --> 00:19:01,235
Only I didn't see her
on account of she was naked.

234
00:19:02,319 --> 00:19:03,570
At least that what she said.

235
00:19:04,154 --> 00:19:06,531
She was behind that rock there
where she was changing.

236
00:19:07,574 --> 00:19:09,034
The young man got kind of jumpy.

237
00:19:09,159 --> 00:19:10,202
Uh-huh.

238
00:19:10,327 --> 00:19:11,411
Asked me if I had a gun.

239
00:19:18,377 --> 00:19:19,962
She probably had a gun
on you the whole time.

240
00:19:20,170 --> 00:19:21,296
That's what I figured.

241
00:19:22,339 --> 00:19:25,342
And if he said one wrong word
or tried to run... bam.

242
00:19:25,717 --> 00:19:27,052
I mean, she would have
shot us both dead.

243
00:19:27,803 --> 00:19:29,263
I'm just thankful he kept his head.

244
00:19:30,347 --> 00:19:32,307
Happen to see what kind
of car they were driving?

245
00:19:32,599 --> 00:19:35,227
Yes, sir. There was
only one car on the bluff.

246
00:19:35,435 --> 00:19:38,188
A dark blue 1990s Dynasty Sedan.

247
00:19:49,032 --> 00:19:50,075
Stay low.

248
00:21:27,172 --> 00:21:28,215
Thank you.

249
00:21:29,007 --> 00:21:30,967
Put these... Put these up there.

250
00:22:00,414 --> 00:22:01,623
Scared you, didn't I?

251
00:22:01,957 --> 00:22:02,999
No.

252
00:22:03,875 --> 00:22:05,502
Saw some cops. Spooked me.

253
00:22:06,044 --> 00:22:07,671
Well, I'm glad I left you the keys.

254
00:22:08,839 --> 00:22:10,715
You're gonna be
a French honey blonde.

255
00:22:10,841 --> 00:22:12,259
- How's that sound?
- Sure.

256
00:22:12,801 --> 00:22:14,803
- Did you get snacks?
- Sure did.

257
00:22:24,479 --> 00:22:26,022
I have something to say.

258
00:22:28,233 --> 00:22:29,526
Come in. Sit down, Dana.

259
00:22:34,072 --> 00:22:35,157
What's going on?

260
00:22:42,789 --> 00:22:44,416
Couldn't sleep last night.

261
00:22:50,338 --> 00:22:51,631
Hmm.

262
00:22:52,632 --> 00:22:54,926
My husband mustn't know.

263
00:22:57,387 --> 00:22:58,555
Mustn't know what?

264
00:23:08,482 --> 00:23:10,692
I sold Lorelei's sister.

265
00:23:12,319 --> 00:23:13,361
A sister?

266
00:23:13,737 --> 00:23:17,032
I don't remember reading anything
about a sister in Lorelei's file.

267
00:23:17,157 --> 00:23:19,534
Because I sold her.

268
00:23:21,745 --> 00:23:23,997
All right, you're gonna have
to help me out here, Dana.

269
00:23:25,248 --> 00:23:29,503
Thirty years ago, I didn't have
the money to raise two girls.

270
00:23:31,546 --> 00:23:33,423
I had substance issues.

271
00:23:36,885 --> 00:23:37,928
Go on.

272
00:23:38,970 --> 00:23:40,096
So after...

273
00:23:42,724 --> 00:23:43,975
their dad left...

274
00:23:46,728 --> 00:23:48,563
I just stopped functioning
you know?

275
00:23:49,272 --> 00:23:54,986
And, um, Lorelei...
she was five.

276
00:23:56,863 --> 00:23:58,657
And she held me up, you know?

277
00:24:01,493 --> 00:24:02,536
But...

278
00:24:04,913 --> 00:24:08,083
Miranda...
that was her name...

279
00:24:10,544 --> 00:24:11,670
She was two.

280
00:24:12,712 --> 00:24:15,340
I mean, what was I gonna do
with a two-year-old?

281
00:24:17,509 --> 00:24:18,552
What did you do?

282
00:24:19,177 --> 00:24:20,220
Well, I knew...

283
00:24:20,887 --> 00:24:23,598
I knew this rich... foreign couple

284
00:24:23,723 --> 00:24:26,726
who... childless.

285
00:24:27,686 --> 00:24:29,396
So we made a deal under
the table.

286
00:24:30,313 --> 00:24:31,648
Why didn't they just adopt her?

287
00:24:31,898 --> 00:24:35,110
We all wanted what we wanted
so we just got it done.

288
00:24:35,902 --> 00:24:37,279
What did you tell Lorelei?

289
00:24:39,739 --> 00:24:40,907
I told her...

290
00:24:43,660 --> 00:24:45,870
I told her all kinds of stuff.

291
00:24:46,079 --> 00:24:47,414
I...

292
00:24:48,540 --> 00:24:50,709
And she never forgave me.

293
00:24:56,590 --> 00:25:01,720
I didn't realize it at the time
but... that day...

294
00:25:03,972 --> 00:25:05,515
I lost two daughters.

295
00:25:06,766 --> 00:25:07,809
Not one.

296
00:25:11,771 --> 00:25:13,106
Want me to get you a tissue?

297
00:25:36,310 --> 00:25:37,353
Hurry up!

298
00:25:49,657 --> 00:25:50,700
Hey there.

299
00:25:51,743 --> 00:25:53,077
Looking for a room.

300
00:25:53,703 --> 00:25:55,830
Place to rest my weary bones.

301
00:25:56,456 --> 00:25:58,040
Been on the road
since New Mexico.

302
00:25:58,166 --> 00:26:02,253
- It's $48 cash, $52 credit.
- Oop. I'll be paying cash.

303
00:26:02,545 --> 00:26:03,588
Okay.

304
00:26:06,591 --> 00:26:09,135
You don't happen
to have one without a television?

305
00:26:09,594 --> 00:26:11,304
Uh, TV's busted in 13.

306
00:26:12,054 --> 00:26:13,431
No discount.

307
00:26:15,767 --> 00:26:16,809
Okay.

308
00:26:26,736 --> 00:26:28,488
- Have a nice day.
- Mm-hmm.

309
00:26:29,197 --> 00:26:30,948
We tried to have
our own children.

310
00:26:31,908 --> 00:26:32,950
I could not.

311
00:26:33,493 --> 00:26:35,453
Why didn't you
just adopt legally?

312
00:26:35,578 --> 00:26:39,332
Well, I was on work visa
from Romania.

313
00:26:39,582 --> 00:26:42,251
And we could not adopt
until we were citizens

314
00:26:42,376 --> 00:26:43,586
and that takes years.

315
00:26:44,378 --> 00:26:47,089
Mr. Kirkland
this is Marta and Virgil Roman.

316
00:26:47,298 --> 00:26:51,302
They're just telling me how they
came to buy Miranda Martins.

317
00:26:52,136 --> 00:26:53,638
You had to see her.

318
00:26:54,013 --> 00:26:56,432
She was in a bad situation.

319
00:26:56,808 --> 00:27:00,895
Virgil and I knew we could
give her a life

320
00:27:01,020 --> 00:27:03,731
full of love and opportunity.

321
00:27:04,148 --> 00:27:08,236
But she turned out to be
a very troubled girl.

322
00:27:08,986 --> 00:27:10,071
Very unhappy.

323
00:27:11,197 --> 00:27:14,992
So when she was in high school
we sent her to a therapist

324
00:27:16,494 --> 00:27:19,080
and she remembered
a lot of things

325
00:27:19,205 --> 00:27:21,707
we thought
she had forgotten.

326
00:27:22,458 --> 00:27:23,501
Her mother?

327
00:27:24,585 --> 00:27:25,628
No.

328
00:27:27,129 --> 00:27:28,965
She remembered
only one name.

329
00:27:29,715 --> 00:27:30,800
Lorelei.

330
00:27:31,759 --> 00:27:33,594
Of course, we found
her sister Lorelei

331
00:27:33,719 --> 00:27:35,137
and reunited them.

332
00:27:36,764 --> 00:27:40,518
The sisters were so happy
and they were so close.

333
00:27:42,019 --> 00:27:44,355
You've never seen
two sisters who were closer.

334
00:27:46,607 --> 00:27:49,277
Where is Miranda now?
We need to talk to her.

335
00:27:51,279 --> 00:27:54,907
She... she was murdered.
She's dead.

336
00:27:58,953 --> 00:28:00,955
It's a shame the TV doesn't work.

337
00:28:06,002 --> 00:28:07,253
Thanks for the dress.

338
00:28:09,005 --> 00:28:10,673
Oh, it's my pleasure.

339
00:28:13,634 --> 00:28:14,802
So, listen, uh...

340
00:28:17,763 --> 00:28:19,390
You gonna tell me
where we're going?

341
00:28:21,100 --> 00:28:23,519
To a cabin my sister and I
used to go to.

342
00:28:24,478 --> 00:28:26,647
- You have a sister?
- I did.

343
00:28:29,233 --> 00:28:30,276
I'm sorry.

344
00:28:31,903 --> 00:28:32,945
Don't be.

345
00:28:33,863 --> 00:28:37,033
Her death was a gift, sort of.

346
00:28:37,700 --> 00:28:41,412
- You wanna explain that?
- You wouldn't understand.

347
00:28:42,830 --> 00:28:44,040
Well, you could try me.

348
00:28:45,124 --> 00:28:46,667
I mean, I... I'd like
to understand.

349
00:28:47,418 --> 00:28:50,254
In case you haven't noticed
healing is not my strong suit.

350
00:28:52,340 --> 00:28:55,426
Losing my sister brought me
into my full reality.

351
00:28:57,011 --> 00:28:59,055
I faced my deepest fear.

352
00:29:00,973 --> 00:29:03,267
I have complete awareness.

353
00:29:05,102 --> 00:29:06,562
Nothing can hurt me.

354
00:29:09,106 --> 00:29:10,483
That's nonsense.
Believe me.

355
00:29:10,942 --> 00:29:12,318
Things can hurt you.

356
00:29:15,279 --> 00:29:16,322
Try me.

357
00:29:19,116 --> 00:29:20,785
Mm. This beer is warm.

358
00:29:23,412 --> 00:29:24,497
I'll get some ice.

359
00:29:33,047 --> 00:29:35,341
Miranda was beautiful
like her sister.

360
00:29:36,217 --> 00:29:38,552
What does the coroner's report
say about the cause of death?

361
00:29:38,678 --> 00:29:39,804
Heatstroke.

362
00:29:39,971 --> 00:29:41,430
After she was raped

363
00:29:42,014 --> 00:29:45,184
she was left chained
inside of an empty warehouse.

364
00:29:45,643 --> 00:29:48,896
Daytime temperatures
reached 120 degrees inside.

365
00:29:49,021 --> 00:29:51,983
Coroner figures
she lasted about two days.

366
00:29:53,484 --> 00:29:54,777
And they never found the killer?

367
00:29:55,861 --> 00:29:56,988
The case is still open.

368
00:29:57,113 --> 00:29:59,073
There's no trace evidence
no witnesses.

369
00:29:59,532 --> 00:30:00,616
Just this.

370
00:30:05,204 --> 00:30:06,872
- Hello?
- "Hey, Lisbon."

371
00:30:08,165 --> 00:30:09,208
I need your help.

372
00:30:10,209 --> 00:30:12,044
I need to take this. Could you...

373
00:30:12,795 --> 00:30:13,963
I'll be right back.

374
00:30:18,217 --> 00:30:22,555
"And this refrain was her song"

375
00:30:24,098 --> 00:30:29,478
"Red sails in the sunset"

376
00:30:30,813 --> 00:30:33,274
Jane, what's going on?
Have you been kidnapped?

377
00:30:33,399 --> 00:30:36,610
Yes. I'm in fear of my life.
I can't talk long.

378
00:30:37,153 --> 00:30:38,696
Did you know Lorelei
had a sister?

379
00:30:39,113 --> 00:30:41,198
Yes. Miranda.
Her mother gave her up.

380
00:30:41,490 --> 00:30:42,533
Where are you?

381
00:30:42,700 --> 00:30:44,827
If she catches me on the phone
she'll kill me.

382
00:30:45,411 --> 00:30:48,039
- What happened to Miranda?
- She was murdered.

383
00:30:48,205 --> 00:30:50,708
Abducted, raped, and left
for dead five years ago.

384
00:30:50,916 --> 00:30:52,126
- "Who did it?"
- They don't know.

385
00:30:52,251 --> 00:30:53,461
They don't even have a suspect.

386
00:30:53,627 --> 00:30:54,670
But listen to this...

387
00:30:54,920 --> 00:30:57,798
"The police kept back
a key detail from the public."

388
00:30:57,923 --> 00:30:58,966
Before Miranda died

389
00:30:59,091 --> 00:31:01,218
she carved a message
into the warehouse floor.

390
00:31:01,343 --> 00:31:02,386
What'd it say?

391
00:31:02,511 --> 00:31:04,430
I'm looking at the crime scene
photo now.

392
00:31:05,014 --> 00:31:06,182
It says "Roy".

393
00:31:09,727 --> 00:31:11,479
I need a copy of that photo.

394
00:31:11,854 --> 00:31:16,150
Uh, Lisbon, yeah. Fax it
to me at this number...

395
00:31:17,026 --> 00:31:18,069
"I'm Katie Riley"

396
00:31:18,194 --> 00:31:20,529
"and I'll be back with more
of your favorite mellow blends"

397
00:31:20,654 --> 00:31:21,864
"right after the news."

398
00:31:22,782 --> 00:31:25,242
"State and federal authorities
have intensified the search"

399
00:31:25,367 --> 00:31:28,162
"for a Sacramento woman,
Lorelei Martins."

400
00:31:28,454 --> 00:31:30,289
Jane, just tell me
where you are.

401
00:31:30,414 --> 00:31:31,457
We can help you.

402
00:31:31,582 --> 00:31:32,750
Just fax it to me.

403
00:31:33,626 --> 00:31:35,086
I gotta go. Gotta go.

404
00:31:47,181 --> 00:31:51,727
"According to police, Martins has
kidnapped CBI consultant, Patrick Jane"

405
00:31:51,852 --> 00:31:54,772
"whose car was found abandoned
by the side of the road."

406
00:32:08,828 --> 00:32:10,162
Everything okay?

407
00:32:12,289 --> 00:32:13,624
Jane just called me.

408
00:32:41,381 --> 00:32:42,549
You filthy liar!

409
00:32:42,959 --> 00:32:44,169
Kidnapped you?

410
00:32:44,335 --> 00:32:45,378
Please...

411
00:32:46,421 --> 00:32:48,757
How dare you? You lied!

412
00:32:53,236 --> 00:32:56,030
I didn't lie. I just
didn't tell you everything.

413
00:32:56,489 --> 00:32:59,617
- Why didn't you tell me?
- I had to protect myself.

414
00:32:59,826 --> 00:33:00,869
Ah!

415
00:33:03,454 --> 00:33:04,497
Oh!

416
00:33:04,622 --> 00:33:06,541
Please. Just stop.

417
00:33:12,922 --> 00:33:14,632
You had me going, Patrick.

418
00:33:21,973 --> 00:33:24,976
For a second there
I almost trusted you.

419
00:33:25,143 --> 00:33:27,270
You should.
You should trust me.

420
00:33:27,395 --> 00:33:30,690
Oh, stop!
Just stop playing the role.

421
00:33:30,815 --> 00:33:32,400
Yes, I play a role
but not with you.

422
00:33:32,525 --> 00:33:34,402
- I'm being honest with you.
- Lies on lies!

423
00:33:34,527 --> 00:33:37,280
Lorelei, listen to me.
You have to listen to me.

424
00:33:37,655 --> 00:33:41,034
Your buddy Red John...
he killed your sister.

425
00:33:42,201 --> 00:33:44,412
- What are you talking about?
- Your sister Miranda.

426
00:33:44,537 --> 00:33:47,040
She wrote a name on the floor
of the warehouse where she died.

427
00:33:47,373 --> 00:33:49,459
The name of the man
who raped and killed her.

428
00:33:49,584 --> 00:33:51,085
It was never released
to the public.

429
00:33:51,210 --> 00:33:52,712
- You're making that up.
- No.

430
00:33:53,296 --> 00:33:55,882
This is a crime scene photo
of your sister's murder

431
00:34:01,471 --> 00:34:03,222
- "Roy".
- Yes, Roy.

432
00:34:03,681 --> 00:34:05,975
We both know
who uses that alias.

433
00:34:08,269 --> 00:34:09,812
I don't understand.

434
00:34:11,022 --> 00:34:12,565
- Where did you get this?
- It doesn't matter.

435
00:34:12,690 --> 00:34:15,068
Red John raped
and killed your sister.

436
00:34:15,234 --> 00:34:16,861
- No.
- He made you a victim

437
00:34:17,028 --> 00:34:18,279
so that he could rescue you.

438
00:34:18,404 --> 00:34:20,281
- No.
- He preyed on your pain.

439
00:34:20,406 --> 00:34:22,408
- No, it's not true.
- Yes. You don't want it to be true.

440
00:34:22,533 --> 00:34:24,369
But it's true, and you can
feel that it's true.

441
00:34:24,494 --> 00:34:25,578
Just stop!

442
00:34:28,289 --> 00:34:30,208
God, you're just
like him, you know that?

443
00:34:30,375 --> 00:34:32,961
- Relentless manipulation.
- I am nothing like him.

444
00:34:33,169 --> 00:34:34,295
How would you know?

445
00:34:35,171 --> 00:34:36,214
I know.

446
00:34:37,757 --> 00:34:40,218
I only wonder why the two of you
didn't become lifelong friends

447
00:34:40,343 --> 00:34:41,886
the moment you shook hands.

448
00:34:47,517 --> 00:34:48,559
Wait!

449
00:34:51,312 --> 00:34:52,355
Where are we going?

450
00:34:52,647 --> 00:34:53,690
We still going to the cabin?

451
00:34:54,273 --> 00:34:56,025
That's where I'm going.
You can go where you like.

452
00:35:09,163 --> 00:35:12,208
We traced Jane's call
to a truck stop motel on Route 99

453
00:35:12,333 --> 00:35:13,376
just north of Chico.

454
00:35:13,501 --> 00:35:15,503
- Right here.
- The fugitive and her hostage were gone

455
00:35:15,628 --> 00:35:17,380
by the time
deputies got to the motel.

456
00:35:33,062 --> 00:35:34,105
"They were moving north."

457
00:35:34,230 --> 00:35:35,898
Let's assume they still are.
Where are they going?

458
00:35:36,024 --> 00:35:39,068
Well, if they take the 97 North
they'll hit the Butter Valley Airport.

459
00:35:39,402 --> 00:35:41,779
One runway. Public use.
Five takeoffs a day.

460
00:35:41,904 --> 00:35:44,157
They might go for a plane.
Okay, lock it down. What else?

461
00:35:44,282 --> 00:35:46,325
I've been going through financial records
for Lorelei's sister.

462
00:35:46,576 --> 00:35:47,952
She owned a cabin in the Sierras

463
00:35:48,077 --> 00:35:49,996
about 200 miles north
of that motel.

464
00:35:50,246 --> 00:35:52,790
From what I can see, the cabin
was never sold after her death.

465
00:35:52,915 --> 00:35:55,209
An anonymous third party has
been paying the taxes on it.

466
00:35:55,334 --> 00:35:56,377
Red John?

467
00:35:56,586 --> 00:35:58,671
Call tactical.
I want a chopper here in ten.

468
00:36:01,007 --> 00:36:03,301
It's just up ahead
at the end of the road.

469
00:36:20,902 --> 00:36:22,528
You go ahead.
I'll get the stuff.

470
00:36:23,237 --> 00:36:24,322
Okay.

471
00:36:37,585 --> 00:36:39,337
The key is under the flower pot.

472
00:37:24,966 --> 00:37:26,259
Welcome.

473
00:37:28,886 --> 00:37:30,304
Well, it's a nice place.

474
00:37:30,847 --> 00:37:31,889
Yeah.

475
00:37:33,850 --> 00:37:35,184
Belonged to my sister.

476
00:37:36,060 --> 00:37:38,271
We used to come here
to forget about the world.

477
00:37:42,525 --> 00:37:43,568
It's safe.

478
00:37:47,947 --> 00:37:50,074
Red John didn't kill her, Patrick.

479
00:37:51,033 --> 00:37:53,077
You'll never convince me
that he did.

480
00:37:55,163 --> 00:37:57,039
I'd kill for a cup of tea right now.

481
00:37:59,876 --> 00:38:01,294
I can make you one.

482
00:38:04,172 --> 00:38:05,214
I'd like that.

483
00:38:06,048 --> 00:38:08,384
- But we can't stay here.
- Why not?

484
00:38:08,843 --> 00:38:11,971
If Miranda bought this place
the police will find it.

485
00:38:12,346 --> 00:38:14,390
They're probably
on their way here right now.

486
00:38:14,515 --> 00:38:16,225
- Then we have to go.
- No, you have to go.

487
00:38:16,559 --> 00:38:18,686
- I'll stay. I'll try and delay them.
- What?

488
00:38:18,811 --> 00:38:20,438
Well, like you said
I'm never gonna convince you

489
00:38:20,563 --> 00:38:22,398
that Red John killed your sister.

490
00:38:22,690 --> 00:38:25,067
You need to go and find out
the truth for yourself.

491
00:38:25,193 --> 00:38:26,235
But, Patrick...

492
00:38:26,360 --> 00:38:27,862
And when you do
when you know the truth...

493
00:38:30,406 --> 00:38:31,699
You know where to find me.

494
00:38:34,118 --> 00:38:35,203
Just call me.

495
00:38:40,208 --> 00:38:41,459
Where are the car keys?

496
00:38:41,626 --> 00:38:42,668
In the car.

497
00:38:46,923 --> 00:38:48,216
Is there a back way
out of here?

498
00:38:48,466 --> 00:38:50,843
Um, there's... no.
There's just fire trails.

499
00:38:50,968 --> 00:38:53,471
Okay. What about this thing?
Does this run?

500
00:38:53,804 --> 00:38:56,390
- It's been on a trickle charge.
- Yeah, it should.

501
00:38:56,641 --> 00:38:58,684
Okay, you take the 4x4
on the fire road.

502
00:38:58,809 --> 00:39:00,811
They won't be looking for that.
I'm gonna cover for you.

503
00:39:00,978 --> 00:39:02,730
You can't stay here, Patrick.

504
00:39:02,980 --> 00:39:05,107
There's no way they'll believe
you were my hostage.

505
00:39:05,316 --> 00:39:06,651
I will make them believe.

506
00:39:06,817 --> 00:39:08,110
You want me to beat you up
or something?

507
00:39:08,236 --> 00:39:10,071
- Knock you out?
- Uh, no, thanks.

508
00:39:19,830 --> 00:39:20,873
You gotta go.

509
00:40:34,405 --> 00:40:36,824
Check the cabin.
Search the surrounding woods.

510
00:40:52,173 --> 00:40:53,215
Jane.

511
00:40:55,343 --> 00:40:56,385
He's okay.

512
00:40:58,429 --> 00:40:59,472
Did you get her?

513
00:40:59,805 --> 00:41:00,848
Not yet.

514
00:41:01,766 --> 00:41:04,602
She's, uh, she's on foot.

515
00:41:04,727 --> 00:41:06,145
Agent Kirkland
Homeland Security.

516
00:41:06,270 --> 00:41:07,730
I need rescue hot
south of Orr Lake

517
00:41:07,855 --> 00:41:09,607
forest Route 42 North 12.

518
00:41:09,815 --> 00:41:11,484
- Who's that guy?
- Don't talk.

519
00:41:12,151 --> 00:41:13,361
Help's on the way.

520
00:41:15,237 --> 00:41:16,322
Hurts.

521
00:41:21,118 --> 00:41:22,661
Shh. It's okay.

522
00:41:35,049 --> 00:41:36,300
You'll never know.

523
00:41:37,009 --> 00:41:38,302
I'll never know what?

524
00:41:38,844 --> 00:41:41,889
Whether I engineered
the escape and abduction.

525
00:41:42,098 --> 00:41:43,808
Trust me. I know.

526
00:41:44,225 --> 00:41:45,393
You don't know.

527
00:41:46,769 --> 00:41:47,937
You just guess.

528
00:41:49,355 --> 00:41:52,108
And you didn't tell your new
best friend, Kirkland, either.

529
00:41:52,233 --> 00:41:53,275
I don't have any evidence.

530
00:41:53,401 --> 00:41:55,403
If I did, I'd put you
in cuffs myself.

531
00:41:55,653 --> 00:41:57,238
- No, you wouldn't.
- Try me.

532
00:42:01,033 --> 00:42:03,536
- What's so funny?
- Nothing. Sorry.

533
00:42:07,832 --> 00:42:09,291
All of it's worth it.

534
00:42:17,508 --> 00:42:20,594
She told me Red John and I
are very much alike.

535
00:42:21,595 --> 00:42:23,389
That it's a wonder
we weren't best friends

536
00:42:23,514 --> 00:42:25,641
from the moment
we shook hands.

537
00:42:26,475 --> 00:42:27,893
You've met Red John?

538
00:42:29,103 --> 00:42:30,146
Yes.

539
00:42:31,230 --> 00:42:32,857
He's someone I know.

